{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added `POST /v1/api-keys/{apiKeyID}/regenerate`, which replaces the key's token in place and returns the API key object with the new `token`. The build and existing tests pass (53 unit packages, 102 integration tests); the new endpoint itself has no test of its own yet.\n\n- **Storage:** `Storage.RegenerateAPIKey(userID, keyID)` in `internal/storage/api_key.go` does a single `UPDATE ... RETURNING` scoped to the user, so the old token stops authenticating as soon as the request completes. It returns `ErrAPIKeyNotFound` when the key does not exist or belongs to another user.\n- **Handler and route:** `regenerateAPIKeyHandler` in `internal/api/api_key_handlers.go`, registered in `internal/api/api.go`. It responds 200 with the key, 400 for an invalid ID, and 404 for a key that is missing or not the caller's.\n- **Client:** added `RegenerateAPIKey` and `RegenerateAPIKeyContext` to `client/client.go`, which the task did not ask for, to match the existing create/delete methods.\n\nOne behaviour to be aware of: regenerating also resets `last_used_at` to null, since the new token has never been used.", "t": 1794463882.491}
